>
  <p><strong>GTA 6 has no instant map teleport.</strong> Instead you call a ride, then either sit through the drive or pay extra to skip it. Several guides agree on how it works.</p>

  <h2>Paradise Taxi (early game)</h2>
  <p>After the opening mission, Gone Fishing, you can call a Paradise Taxi from your phone's Contacts. It charges the fare from the cash you're carrying, and it's your only ride service until RydeMe arrives.</p>

  <h2>RydeMe</h2>
  <p>RydeMe unlocks when you finish the BuckMe mission and get your bank account. The app is then added to your phone on its own. Fares come out of your bank account and grow with distance. You can ride to a safehouse, your map marker, or a spot you pick on the map.</p>

  <h2>Skipping the ride</h2>
  <p>Staying in the car takes about as long as driving. Skipping adds a flat $100 on top of the fare, for taxis and RydeMe alike. On one guide's controls that's holding L2/LT and pressing Triangle/Y.</p>

